# The Docker build context is the repository root (deploy/docker/agent.Dockerfile).
# This is an allowlist: only what the Rust build needs gets in, so nothing
# secret (secrets/, .env files, keys, databases) can enter the context, even a
# file added later (ADR-0014). The desktop app's Rust side is a workspace member, so
# cargo needs it to load the workspace, though the agent never builds it (ADR-0017).
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!.cargo/config.toml
!crates/
!apps/desktop/src-tauri/

# Build output inside a crate, if any, and tauri-build's generated schemas.
crates/**/target
apps/desktop/src-tauri/target
apps/desktop/src-tauri/gen

# .gitignore's secret patterns again, at any depth: the last matching rule
# wins, and crates/ and src-tauri/ are allowed as a whole.
**/.env*
**/*.pem
**/*.key
**/secrets
**/*.db*
